---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import StatusChit from '../components/StatusChit.astro';
---

<Site
  title="Hotkeys and Stream Deck"
  description="Drive your Vellum HUD from hotkeys or a Stream Deck. Every input sends the same command, and everything stays on your machine."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Control</p>
      <h1>Hands on the game,<br /><em>not the mouse.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        During a session you shouldn't have to dig through OBS to mark a point of HP. Vellum takes
        input from a click, a hotkey or a Stream Deck key, and they all send the same command.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ways-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Three ways in</p>
        <h2 id="ways-h">Pick the one that fits your desk.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card lead">
          <div class="card-top"><h3>Click</h3><StatusChit status="live" /></div>
          <p class="small">
            Click a pip on the HUD in OBS's Interact window. It works today and stays as the
            fallback.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-top"><h3>Hotkeys</h3><StatusChit status="live" /></div>
          <p class="small">
            Load the Vellum script in OBS (Tools, Scripts) and bind keys in OBS's Hotkeys settings.
            They work while OBS is in the background.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-top"><h3>Stream Deck</h3><StatusChit status="live" /></div>
          <p class="small">
            Point Stream Deck's built-in Hotkey action at the Vellum hotkeys, or install the plugin
          for keys that show your values.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="deck-h">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">A starting layout</p>
        <h2 id="deck-h">Six keys cover a session.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The commands are relative, so two quick presses always add up to two. Bind as many or as
          few as you like.
        </p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Hope up and down</li>
          <li>Mark HP and Stress</li>
          <li>Spend Armor</li>
          <li>Toggle a condition</li>
          <li>Switch frames mid-session</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="keys" aria-label="Example Stream Deck layout">
        <div class="key" style="--key: var(--color-signal)">
          <b>+1</b><span>Hope</span><kbd>Ctrl Alt 1</kbd>
        </div>
        <div class="key" style="--key: var(--color-signal)">
          <b>−1</b><span>Hope</span><kbd>Ctrl Alt 2</kbd>
        </div>
        <div class="key" style="--key: var(--color-hit)">
          <b>+1</b><span>HP</span><kbd>Ctrl Alt 3</kbd>
        </div>
        <div class="key" style="--key: var(--color-stress)">
          <b>+1</b><span>Stress</span><kbd>Ctrl Alt 4</kbd>
        </div>
        <div class="key" style="--key: var(--color-armor)">
          <b>−1</b><span>Armor</span><kbd>Ctrl Alt 5</kbd>
        </div>
        <div class="key" style="--key: var(--color-hit)">
          <b>Vuln</b><span>Toggle</span><kbd>Ctrl Alt 6</kbd>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="plugin-h">
    <div class="wrap split flip">
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="status-line"><StatusChit status="live" /></div>
        <h2 id="plugin-h">Keys that show your stats.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The Vellum Stream Deck plugin draws your live Hope, HP, Stress, Armor and Fear on the keys
          themselves, lights condition keys while they're on, and turns dials on Stream Deck + into
          stat knobs.
        </p>
        <p class="small">
          It listens on your own computer for the Vellum HUD in OBS. No OBS WebSocket, no password,
          and nothing goes through the internet.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/downloads/vellum.streamDeckPlugin" download
            >Download the plugin</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card lead">
        <h3>How the input path works</h3>
        <p class="small">
          Every input becomes one typed command, such as "add 1 to Hope". The HUD is the only thing
          that changes your sheet: it applies the command, saves it, and redraws. A key press and a
          click take the same path, so they can never disagree.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="cta-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="cta-h">Set it up</h2>
        <p class="lede">The guide walks through the script, the bindings and Stream Deck.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/control/">Hotkeys and Stream Deck guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
